WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.085
-Excuse me.
-Hi.

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:03.128
-I am looking for
a lady's suit.

00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:04.671
-Okay. What kind?

00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:06.298
-A successful business suit.

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:09.593
-Ooh! Like Connie Chung,
or like "Dynasty"?

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.724
-This episode is about a young
woman trying to figure out

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:17.267
a way to make ends meet
for her and her son,

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:19.686
and ends up opening
a cookie business

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.190
by selling in a very traditional
"Ugandan marketplace" way.

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:24.566
-You go out there like that?

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.901
-That's gonna make you famous!

00:00:27.903 --> 00:00:30.531
-The character is actually based on

00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:33.116
a real story,
Elizabeth Kizito,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.370
who is a Ugandan woman who came here
and started her own business

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.163
selling cookies in Louisville.

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:40.999
-How's that staying on
your head right now?

00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:42.709
-African magic.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:48.465
-So, I'm an immigrant, and I
came to the States for college,

00:00:48.549 --> 00:00:51.426
and so I feel like I brought
my own life experience,

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.136
since I know what it is
to be in this country,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.681
I know what it is to want to
succeed in this country.

00:00:58.851 --> 00:01:01.270
-The talent on this episode
is fantastic.

00:01:01.353 --> 00:01:03.856
I think Kemi and Innocent,
who plays her son,

00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:06.358
they bring a sense of
authenticity and playfulness

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:09.027
that is really infectious
to the crew and the set.

00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:15.993
-The crew's amazing.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.828
From the props
to the wardrobe, everything,

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.955
it just goes through
this filter of

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:21.999
"Are we doing it as
realistically as we can?"

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.250
The episode that
we're shooting right now,

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:24.293
the toe polish wasn't right,

00:01:24.376 --> 00:01:26.044
and the hair and makeup people

00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:28.714
caught it and just immediately
started scrubbing the toes

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:30.883
right before we started shooting
'cause that color nail polish

00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:32.759
did not exist in 1981
in Louisville.

00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:33.844
-And cut.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.930
-If people feel a connection to
Beatrice as a person,

00:01:37.014 --> 00:01:40.726
and can see her as a full
character, that would be ideal.

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:43.145
Somebody who's not
a perfect human being,

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:46.064
but somebody who has dreams
and obstacles just like the rest of us.

00:01:46.148 --> 00:01:49.526
-It's a beautiful story
and a beautiful TV show

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.361
that, week after week,
will remind you

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:55.157
of all these beautiful cultures that
these people bring in to this country.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.576
-My mommy is the cookie lady.

